# Introduction to graph

A graph in data structures is a non-linear way to represent relationships
between entities (objects) using vertices (nodes) and connecting edges (links)

Types of Graph:
1. Directed Graph   2. Undirected Graph

* Directed graph contains undirected edges, nodes/vertex.
* Directed graph contains directed edges which may be unidirectional/bidirectional.

> Graph may be CYCLIC or ACYCLIC.

# Degree in Graph:
    The degree of a vertex (or node) is the number of edges connected to it.
    Note: Total degree of a graph= 2 x (no of edges).
# For Directed graph:
    1. In Degree: No of incoming edges on a vertex.
    2. Out Degree: No of outgoing edges on a vertex.

# Edge Weight:
    * The value assign to the edge is called edge weight.
    * If weight is not assign to any edge then will consider it as 1.


